WEBVTT

00:01.960 --> 00:05.230
Everyone back in Ikajima Town, are you well?

00:05.790 --> 00:07.860
The weather in Tokyo has been so warm lately,

00:08.360 --> 00:10.750
you don't even need a jacket on most days.

00:11.610 --> 00:17.590
With the midterms coming up soon,
everyone at school's studying hard.

00:17.590 --> 00:20.560
As you'd expect from
an elite prep school in Tokyo,

00:20.560 --> 00:23.550
the students are hard workers
and competitive,

00:23.550 --> 00:26.150
which keeps me on my toes every day.

00:26.150 --> 00:29.750
That's right... They're hard workers,
and they're very competitive.

00:30.800 --> 00:33.090
That decides our rosters for each sport.

00:33.090 --> 00:37.020
School only runs half the day during exams, but
we're not allowed to practice after school.

00:37.020 --> 00:40.430
So team practice sessions will
have to wait until after exams.

00:40.900 --> 00:43.940
That doesn't leave us much time,
but let's do as much as we can.

00:44.530 --> 00:48.110
Also, this part is a request
from me personally.

00:48.110 --> 00:52.110
I want us to be in it to win the whole thing.

00:52.450 --> 00:57.070
Yeah, we need an overall objective
on top of goals for each event.

00:57.070 --> 01:00.120
We'll want to release all
that pent-up exam stress, too.

01:00.120 --> 01:04.120
Why don't we show a united front, huh?

01:04.830 --> 01:07.200
We can start the weekend after exams.

01:07.200 --> 01:09.230
Aim for the top!

01:09.230 --> 01:10.570
Let's do this!

01:10.570 --> 01:11.750
Yeah!

01:12.190 --> 01:13.020
If you play a sport, please take
the reins and set up a practice menu.

01:13.020 --> 01:16.570
Do people here really get
this amped up over events?!
If you play a sport, please take
the reins and set up a practice menu.

01:16.570 --> 01:17.290
If you play a sport, please take
the reins and set up a practice menu.

02:49.820 --> 02:51.960
Me? Table tennis.

02:51.960 --> 02:55.770
I don't want the slightest possibility
of messing up in a team sport.

02:55.770 --> 02:58.790
I can't believe you two picked volleyball.

02:58.790 --> 03:03.250
What's the point of making us compete in
stuff that won't affect our entrance exams?

03:03.250 --> 03:05.830
To hell with the insecurities
of the unathletic, huh?

03:05.830 --> 03:08.750
It's all machismo-driven mumbo-jumbo!

03:08.750 --> 03:10.090
Makocchan...

03:10.090 --> 03:14.770
People like her, who'd lead the unhealthiest
lifestyle without school sports,

03:14.770 --> 03:17.130
are the ones who need this the most.

03:17.940 --> 03:23.140
But honestly, someone had to
say it, and I'm glad she did.

03:23.140 --> 03:26.300
That's uncharacteristically
pessimistic, coming from you.

03:26.770 --> 03:31.460
This might surprise you, but the truth is...

03:32.170 --> 03:34.420
I'm terrible at sports!

03:34.420 --> 03:35.360
Uh huh.

03:35.360 --> 03:37.910
I've somehow kept it under wraps so far,

03:37.910 --> 03:42.050
but I'm a class officer!
I can't destroy our morale by sucking!

03:42.050 --> 03:46.170
Whew... That should do it...
for an easy, casual jog...

03:46.170 --> 03:47.740
So slow!

03:47.740 --> 03:49.370
Good point.

03:49.980 --> 03:51.580
Wanna put in some individual practice?

03:51.580 --> 03:53.890
I can help you during lunch break.

03:53.890 --> 03:55.140
You will?!

03:55.140 --> 03:57.050
But wait, volleyball, huh?

03:57.050 --> 03:59.220
Have any of the other girls played?

03:59.220 --> 04:01.730
Why don't you try asking
one of them for help?

04:02.130 --> 04:03.050
Oh.

04:03.680 --> 04:05.240
Your butt's sticking out.

04:05.680 --> 04:09.360
I said lower your hips, not stick
your butt out. Big difference!

04:09.360 --> 04:13.560
You can't stop the ball's momentum unless
you relax and keep your body flexible.

04:13.560 --> 04:15.000
I see...

04:15.000 --> 04:15.770
Like this?

04:15.770 --> 04:17.610
Your feet are all wrong again.

04:18.220 --> 04:20.780
How did I get roped into this?

04:21.190 --> 04:23.930
Man, the restroom's
pretty far from here, huh?

04:24.350 --> 04:26.650
Okay, you're doing better now!

04:26.650 --> 04:28.430
Let's try another receive.

04:29.150 --> 04:30.400
I see.

04:31.190 --> 04:33.710
Sounds like you're in for an uphill battle.

04:34.090 --> 04:36.860
Sorry... I'm so sorry...

04:37.580 --> 04:40.650
Hey, everyone has their
strengths and weaknesses.

04:40.650 --> 04:42.670
You can tutor me in
classic literature in return.

04:42.670 --> 04:46.090
Of course! Ask me anything!

04:46.090 --> 04:49.720
How about you, Egashira-san?
Are you bad in any subjects?

04:49.720 --> 04:53.140
I could stand to improve my math, I guess?

04:53.820 --> 04:57.420
But then again, I could get used to this...

04:58.800 --> 05:00.220
As a treat!

05:22.630 --> 05:23.960
Here, for you two.

05:23.960 --> 05:26.540
Wow, you didn't have to!

05:26.540 --> 05:30.990
You're helping me out,
so Nao-cha— I mean, my aunt insisted.

05:30.990 --> 05:32.140
Thanks.

05:32.960 --> 05:33.770
Urk.

05:34.100 --> 05:36.000
It's all sweet junk.

05:37.390 --> 05:39.630
I'm good with just this.

05:39.630 --> 05:41.920
We can share the rest in class.

05:41.920 --> 05:43.440
You sure you don't want the bread?

05:44.030 --> 05:47.310
I mean, your lunches all look like this!

05:47.310 --> 05:48.640
A girly girl's lunch.

05:48.640 --> 05:50.570
I'm not a big eater.

05:51.420 --> 05:54.450
I'm controlling myself because
I gain weight easily, damn it!

05:55.450 --> 05:59.850
Bet it was a culture shock
for the guys who got school lunches.

05:59.850 --> 06:03.330
Surprised me, too. Everyone has
big appetites where I'm from.

06:03.330 --> 06:04.020
He's still an enigma,
Surprised me, too. Everyone has
big appetites where I'm from.

06:04.020 --> 06:05.170
Oh, really?
He's still an enigma,

06:05.170 --> 06:05.750
Yeah.

06:05.750 --> 06:07.970
but it looks like Shima-kun
really is a nice person.
What sides do you like in your lunch?

06:07.970 --> 06:09.050
Me?
but it looks like Shima-kun
really is a nice person.

06:09.050 --> 06:09.780
It's not exactly a side,
but I love pickled plum.

06:09.780 --> 06:12.180
Lucky you, Iwakura-san.
It's not exactly a side,
but I love pickled plum.

06:12.180 --> 06:12.580
It's not exactly a side,
but I love pickled plum.

06:12.580 --> 06:13.390
He accepts you for who you are.
It's not exactly a side,
but I love pickled plum.

06:13.390 --> 06:14.560
He accepts you for who you are.

06:16.010 --> 06:18.640
You haven't had to deny yourself
your favorite foods,

06:19.140 --> 06:21.430
fight your way into a glamorous club,

06:21.430 --> 06:23.510
or surround yourself with glamorous people.

06:25.090 --> 06:28.800
You haven't had to put in
all that effort.

06:31.670 --> 06:35.410
Sorry! A teacher asked me
to do something earlier!

06:35.740 --> 06:39.950
Can you two go ahead without me today?
I might not make it at all.

06:39.950 --> 06:40.830
Got it.

06:40.830 --> 06:42.480
Ugh...

06:42.480 --> 06:43.680
Let's do this!

06:43.680 --> 06:45.570
The two of us, alone?

06:50.940 --> 06:51.720
Huh?

06:52.080 --> 06:54.640
Their shoes have blue highlights,
so they must be third-years.

06:55.080 --> 06:58.030
Isn't this the first-years' day
to use the gym?

06:58.030 --> 07:00.270
We can use the space over there.

07:01.990 --> 07:04.520
Hey, you've gotten pretty good at returns!

07:04.520 --> 07:05.800
Heh, haven't I?

07:05.800 --> 07:06.710
There!
Heh, haven't I?

07:06.710 --> 07:07.150
There!

07:07.150 --> 07:07.990
Got it!

07:17.130 --> 07:19.370
Where do you think you're throwing it, man?

07:19.370 --> 07:21.850
My bad! It slipped out!

07:24.070 --> 07:25.190
Excuse me!

07:26.530 --> 07:29.070
Us first-years have the gym today!

07:29.070 --> 07:29.940
Hey!

07:32.150 --> 07:33.090
Right.

07:35.870 --> 07:37.180
What's up?

07:37.180 --> 07:39.520
Nothing. Here it comes.

07:43.590 --> 07:46.700
It's back. I haven't had
this feeling in a while.

07:50.650 --> 07:52.480
Shirai! Shibamoto!

07:53.030 --> 07:55.530
They're first-year girls! Shame on you!

07:55.530 --> 07:56.510
Ack.

07:56.910 --> 07:58.890
Get outta here already.

07:58.890 --> 07:59.910
Our bad, man.

07:59.910 --> 08:02.930
We get it! Stop calling us out like that!

08:08.050 --> 08:09.200
I'm okay.

08:11.750 --> 08:13.590
That aside...

08:13.590 --> 08:15.470
Shirai... Shibamoto...

08:16.440 --> 08:19.970
You know what? You two just made the list!

08:19.970 --> 08:22.520
The List of Mika.

08:22.520 --> 08:25.510
A mental notepad that contains
the names of every person

08:25.510 --> 08:28.730
who dared to get on Egashira-san's bad side.

08:29.390 --> 08:31.700
Yikes, that was scary.

08:31.700 --> 08:33.570
People like that really exist, huh?

08:33.570 --> 08:35.100
And you!

08:35.100 --> 08:37.270
Don't put yourself in that kind of situation!

08:37.270 --> 08:39.760
Next time, just tell a teacher!

08:39.760 --> 08:41.040
B-But...

08:41.040 --> 08:44.480
Putting guys like that on blast
is not the only way!

08:44.480 --> 08:46.190
If they're scary, keep your distance!

08:46.190 --> 08:47.540
Okay...

08:47.540 --> 08:53.530
But wasn't Fukuda-san cool?
He really told them off!

08:53.530 --> 08:55.800
Huh? You know him?

08:56.190 --> 08:59.600
Nah, I just got his name from his shoes.

09:03.320 --> 09:05.480
Hm? Egashira-san?

09:07.250 --> 09:09.140
That's the difference between us.

09:10.380 --> 09:13.790
While I learn the names
of people who piss me off,

09:14.580 --> 09:20.120
Iwakura-san remembers the name
of someone who was kind to her.

09:22.620 --> 09:24.540
Ah! I knew it!

09:24.980 --> 09:28.850
I figured you were up to something
because you kept running off during lunch break!

09:28.850 --> 09:30.670
You've been practicing in secret, huh?

09:30.670 --> 09:33.640
I picked volleyball too!
You could've invited me!

09:33.640 --> 09:34.670
But...

09:35.200 --> 09:38.260
The truth is, I suck at sports.

09:38.260 --> 09:39.810
Uh, yeah? We know?

09:41.210 --> 09:41.720
I'm not a stunning beauty,

09:41.720 --> 09:43.730
So? Gotten any better?
I'm not a stunning beauty,

09:44.430 --> 09:45.190
I think I've gotten used to
keeping my eyes on the ball.

09:45.190 --> 09:47.500
or a pure, straightforward person.
I think I've gotten used to
keeping my eyes on the ball.

09:50.920 --> 09:54.600
Who in the world is ever going to choose me?

09:56.700 --> 09:59.190
One sec. I'll be right down.

09:59.190 --> 10:00.470
Okay.

10:00.470 --> 10:02.770
Murashige-san used to be
on the volleyball team, too.

10:02.770 --> 10:04.830
So why did you come to me?

10:05.810 --> 10:09.210
I guess I have always been nasty to you, huh?

10:09.720 --> 10:11.690
So you didn't mind troubling me? Is that it?

10:12.630 --> 10:14.590
What? I didn't...

10:18.340 --> 10:24.600
W-Well, I did think you
were a bit harsh at times.

10:24.600 --> 10:26.080
You did, huh?

10:26.080 --> 10:29.100
But looking back...

10:29.890 --> 10:34.810
You never lied to me.
You just didn't mince words.

10:35.730 --> 10:41.230
So I figured you wouldn't sugarcoat
things with volleyball, either.

10:41.620 --> 10:46.750
You know, there's more to teaching
than simply answering questions.

10:47.110 --> 10:49.620
And you did teach me well.

10:50.550 --> 10:56.690
You've worked really hard to
get this good, and it shows.

11:06.990 --> 11:10.400
Uh, you know I'm not praising
your personality, right?

11:11.330 --> 11:12.690
I know, I know!

11:12.690 --> 11:14.480
You've got a sharp tongue yourself!

11:14.730 --> 11:18.970
Sorry! I don't have my tracks with me
today, but I can do some light tosses.

11:18.970 --> 11:21.120
I'm just here to heckle.

11:22.090 --> 11:24.070
Can you come tomorrow too, Murashige-san?

11:24.790 --> 11:25.490
Sure.

11:25.490 --> 11:28.010
Then help me teach Iwakura-san.

11:28.010 --> 11:30.390
Kurume-san, you take videos
and jot down notes.

11:30.390 --> 11:31.080
Huh?

11:32.060 --> 11:35.840
Just so you know,
once I get serious, that's that!

11:35.840 --> 11:38.760
I only play to win, you hear me?

11:38.760 --> 11:40.010
Wow.

11:40.690 --> 11:41.960
Shima-kun.

11:41.960 --> 11:44.910
What's going on? We doing
a drill sergeant routine today?

11:44.910 --> 11:46.720
I wanted in.

11:47.500 --> 11:49.220
Done with your errand?

11:49.220 --> 11:50.010
Yep.

11:50.010 --> 11:52.990
But it looks like you have enough help,
so maybe I'll head back.

11:52.990 --> 11:55.740
C-Come on, we don't have
much time! Let's get started!

11:55.740 --> 11:56.970
Okay.

11:58.090 --> 11:59.310
Egashira-san.

12:01.460 --> 12:02.780
You can do it.

12:04.110 --> 12:05.320
"You can do it"...

12:07.670 --> 12:08.760
You can do it.

12:10.950 --> 12:14.710
We'll work on your passing
before team practice begins!

12:14.710 --> 12:17.340
Get your act together, Class Officer!

12:17.340 --> 12:18.110
Yes, ma'am!

12:24.520 --> 12:26.010
There we go!

12:26.010 --> 12:27.840
Braiding complete.

12:27.840 --> 12:30.350
You look so cute, Makocchan!

12:30.350 --> 12:31.670
Thanks.

12:31.670 --> 12:33.140
You're welcome.

12:37.850 --> 12:41.400
Are you happy? Bet you are,
since you're cuter now.

12:42.650 --> 12:43.960
I'm right, aren't I?

12:43.960 --> 12:44.920
Ugh, shut up!

12:44.920 --> 12:47.450
She can do that all by herself?

12:47.450 --> 12:50.140
I'm not saying you need to go that far...

12:51.410 --> 12:54.410
But that topknot is just not it.

12:54.410 --> 12:55.580
Huh?

12:55.970 --> 12:58.520
It was my way of preparing
myself for battle...

12:58.520 --> 13:02.000
Yeah, no, it's way too uncool.
Do you think you're home or something?

13:03.860 --> 13:04.550
There.

13:07.510 --> 13:09.580
I want those hairpins back
when we're done, okay?

13:16.850 --> 13:18.760
Thanks, Mika-chan!

13:18.760 --> 13:19.780
I'm so happy!

13:19.780 --> 13:21.230
Yeah, yeah.

13:21.640 --> 13:24.630
Ooh, your forehead looks cute, Mitsumi.

13:24.630 --> 13:26.570
Heh-heh!

13:26.570 --> 13:29.440
Today's class match day!

13:30.620 --> 13:31.850
Go, go!

13:33.190 --> 13:34.200
Nice!

13:34.200 --> 13:35.620
Stay calm!

13:36.320 --> 13:37.320
You can do this!

13:37.320 --> 13:38.630
Nice!

13:38.630 --> 13:40.230
Yay!

13:42.530 --> 13:43.790
Fight!

13:45.230 --> 13:46.630
Game, set, and match!

13:47.910 --> 13:49.960
Yay, we made it to the knockouts!

13:50.390 --> 13:52.170
We're doing great, huh?

13:52.170 --> 13:54.520
Our weekend practices are paying off.

13:54.520 --> 13:56.140
Aim for gold!

13:56.140 --> 13:58.250
Let's do this!

14:02.270 --> 14:05.610
This is why I hate these
stupid class matches!

14:05.610 --> 14:07.320
Don't mind it.

14:08.170 --> 14:12.440
We'll avenge you, Makocchan.
Come on, let's have lunch.

14:12.440 --> 14:16.950
A few wins, and she thinks
she's a volleyball pro now.

14:17.940 --> 14:20.260
It's pretty boring when we're not playing.

14:20.260 --> 14:22.550
Let's go cheer on the others after we eat.

14:22.550 --> 14:24.380
I brought us all something.

14:25.340 --> 14:28.010
I made pickled veggies!

14:28.010 --> 14:30.140
Wow, you made these?

14:30.140 --> 14:32.020
I figured we could use the sodium.

14:32.020 --> 14:33.830
Digging in!

14:34.390 --> 14:37.370
I think I'll give some to
Shima-kun and the team, too.

14:37.780 --> 14:39.550
We're going to go watch
the basketball, right?

14:40.290 --> 14:41.900
Hmm...

14:42.610 --> 14:45.260
I don't know if you'll be able to.

14:50.610 --> 14:52.480
Check this out, Mukai.

14:52.480 --> 14:56.490
Apparently, guys are thirty percent
cooler when playing sports.

14:56.490 --> 14:57.750
That so?

14:58.060 --> 15:00.500
Time to line up. Let's kick their butts.

15:00.500 --> 15:01.500
Yeah!

15:02.680 --> 15:05.250
She may be here right now...

15:05.250 --> 15:08.460
My future love, my amore!

15:08.460 --> 15:10.660
Good luck, Shima-kun!

15:10.660 --> 15:12.510
Hope springs eternal.

15:12.910 --> 15:14.940
Wow, so many people here.

15:14.940 --> 15:18.420
I'm guessing most of them
are here for Shima-kun.

15:19.390 --> 15:21.250
Is Number 5 Shima-kun?

15:21.250 --> 15:23.730
Wow, he really is cute!

15:23.730 --> 15:25.350
Even the upperclassmen?

15:34.660 --> 15:36.450
Nice one, Yamada!

15:36.450 --> 15:38.120
Go get 'em!

15:38.120 --> 15:40.330
Let's gooo!

15:40.330 --> 15:42.680
He could have taken that shot himself.

15:42.680 --> 15:44.960
The other team is all newbies,

15:44.960 --> 15:45.720
so he took a step back
to let his friend shine.

15:45.720 --> 15:47.500
Let's get another.
so he took a step back
to let his friend shine.

15:47.500 --> 15:48.210
so he took a step back
to let his friend shine.

15:48.710 --> 15:51.300
Squee! He's so cool!

15:52.060 --> 15:53.180
The rich get richer!

15:53.880 --> 15:54.300
You can do it!

15:54.300 --> 15:55.340
Shima-kun really is popular.
You can do it!

15:55.340 --> 15:56.870
Shima-kun really is popular.

15:56.870 --> 15:58.340
Shima-kun!
Shima-kun really is popular.

15:58.340 --> 16:03.940
Not that I didn't know, but it really
shows during an event like this.

16:09.420 --> 16:10.890
Class 3 wins!

16:16.260 --> 16:17.760
Aren't you giving them to him?

16:17.760 --> 16:22.320
Nah! I can't really go talk
to him right now, can I?

16:22.320 --> 16:24.960
I wonder where Yuzu-chan and Makocchan are.

16:25.510 --> 16:28.450
I guess even Mitsumi can read this room.

16:29.590 --> 16:33.170
Oh, wanna head back?
Our next match is coming up.

16:33.170 --> 16:36.670
Shima's a good guy, so why
do I feel so empty inside?!

16:36.670 --> 16:37.540
Yamada.

16:38.890 --> 16:41.220
Great shot. That was really cool.

16:42.570 --> 16:45.470
Viva class matches!

16:45.470 --> 16:47.020
Happy for you, man.

16:47.410 --> 16:49.350
Huh, Iwakura-san.

16:49.350 --> 16:50.330
Sousuke should be—

16:50.330 --> 16:52.440
It's fine. I only came to watch.

16:59.990 --> 17:03.800
Yeah, no way she could give
anything to him back there.

17:03.800 --> 17:08.000
If she'd even talked to him, the other girls
would've been like, "Who the hell is she?!"

17:08.000 --> 17:13.150
Yeah, and then they would've gone,
"She even brought him something! No way!"

17:13.150 --> 17:16.090
Y-You thought so, too? Close call.

17:16.090 --> 17:19.000
Is Shima-kun that popular?

17:19.000 --> 17:22.300
Crazy, huh? It's still only June...

17:22.600 --> 17:24.310
Kanechika-senpai!

17:24.310 --> 17:25.670
Hello!

17:25.670 --> 17:27.150
Hello, girls.

17:27.150 --> 17:30.050
Uh, which sport are you
participating in, Senpai?

17:30.050 --> 17:31.380
Soccer.

17:31.380 --> 17:35.450
But I'm just a sub, so I was making
rice balls up in the Home Ec. room.

17:35.450 --> 17:39.620
I'll never be useful in anything physical,
no matter how hard I try.

17:39.950 --> 17:44.500
So I'm focusing on looking after the team's
energy levels and conditioning.

17:44.500 --> 17:47.330
They're freshly made,
so all of you, have one.

17:47.750 --> 17:49.630
Don't worry. I used plastic wrap.

17:51.620 --> 17:54.270
Never thought about offering
the whole team the pickles, huh?

17:54.270 --> 17:55.630
Thank you!

17:56.330 --> 17:57.970
Let's sit down there and eat these.

17:57.970 --> 18:00.420
Oh, then we can eat these too.

18:00.420 --> 18:03.050
Shima-kun must be lonely.

18:03.050 --> 18:03.960
Huh?

18:03.960 --> 18:08.480
Well, I've never been popular,
so I'm just guessing.

18:08.480 --> 18:10.860
He may act the same as he always does,

18:10.860 --> 18:14.070
but maybe people tend to
keep their distance from him.

18:14.070 --> 18:17.280
Lonely? Who, Shima-kun?

18:18.340 --> 18:25.160
He's the first friend I made in Tokyo,
and I see him as a really good friend.

18:25.980 --> 18:29.690
But part of me was afraid he
didn't see me the same way

18:30.490 --> 18:35.160
and assumed I was the lonely one.

18:36.270 --> 18:41.770
Why did he ask me to be
his friend in the first place?

18:45.740 --> 18:48.060
Th-They're good!

18:48.460 --> 18:53.060
They have someone who made starter on
the volleyball team as a first-year! No fair!

18:53.890 --> 18:57.690
Heh-heh. It's my serve now.

19:05.490 --> 19:06.660
Gah!

19:07.250 --> 19:09.560
You're targeting a newbie with jump serves?

19:09.560 --> 19:10.670
That's dirty!

19:10.670 --> 19:12.960
Shaddup! All's fair in sport and war!

19:12.960 --> 19:15.690
She's planning to finish
the game off with her serves.

19:15.690 --> 19:19.330
Hang in there, Mitsumi! We'll do
our best to scoop up your receives!

19:19.330 --> 19:21.090
O-Okay...

19:21.090 --> 19:24.360
You practiced so much! You can do this!

19:28.280 --> 19:29.350
That's right.

19:30.650 --> 19:35.020
I was going full-tilt on the day
of the entrance ceremony, too.

19:45.550 --> 19:49.200
So much so that I was just
running around in circles.

19:49.750 --> 19:53.960
I probably was a huge bother
to Shima-kun on that day.

19:54.740 --> 19:58.180
I was "the puker," but he paid it no mind

19:58.180 --> 20:00.930
and reached out to me...

20:19.070 --> 20:22.300
Whoa! Awesome!

20:28.600 --> 20:30.580
Second place...

20:30.580 --> 20:32.780
This sucks!

20:33.160 --> 20:37.320
But it was so much fun. We did our best.

20:37.320 --> 20:38.580
Yeah.

20:38.580 --> 20:41.460
Looks like the boys made
the final in basketball.

20:41.810 --> 20:43.180
It's about to start.

20:45.870 --> 20:48.230
I'm going to run there.

20:48.230 --> 20:50.380
I couldn't focus on
cheering for them earlier.

20:50.380 --> 20:52.430
And I'm going to hand these over, too!

20:53.410 --> 20:55.440
Whoa.

20:55.800 --> 20:57.700
She's so tough.

20:57.700 --> 21:01.200
I'm kinda envious that she can
ultimately make that choice.

21:02.640 --> 21:07.410
Why does it sound like you like
Shima-kun too, Egashira-san?

21:07.410 --> 21:09.110
Wait, no!

21:09.110 --> 21:12.350
Sure, I think he's hot, but so do you!

21:12.350 --> 21:16.210
Besides, we've only been going
to school together for two months.

21:17.090 --> 21:22.060
Well, even Mitsumi only has
"We're just friends" vibes right now.

21:22.060 --> 21:24.280
They're so tight, though.

21:24.280 --> 21:25.950
Let's go cheer them on, too.

21:27.140 --> 21:28.860
They're not wrong, but...

21:29.950 --> 21:32.170
When you fall in love,

21:32.970 --> 21:36.190
sometimes it's because you find
something in them that you don't have.

21:36.190 --> 21:37.900
Give 'em hell!

21:42.970 --> 21:44.640
And maybe, just maybe,

21:46.470 --> 21:48.490
whatever it is Shima-kun wishes he had...

21:48.490 --> 21:50.540
Heck yeah!

21:52.130 --> 21:54.360
You're awesome, bro!

21:54.360 --> 21:57.600
She might just have it.

22:01.550 --> 22:03.380
That's the feeling I get.

22:05.630 --> 22:07.250
What's this?

22:07.250 --> 22:08.530
Pickled veggies!
